    "heading": "Try two edits at once",
    "prose": [
      "Add notes from both tabs at once Open the board in two tabs. In each one, type a different note into Went well and click Add in both at the same moment. Both notes show up, in both tabs, in the same order. Nothing is lost.",
      "Each note uses a different key Notes are keyed by note id in an OR-map, so two adds write two different keys — there's nothing for them to collide over. Store the board as a plain map keyed by column instead, and you'd get one note back, not two: a map with one key per column has one slot per column, so the second note overwrites the first — that's what “last write wins” means. Keying by note id means there's no shared slot to overwrite."
    ],
